 as reported.\n\n### Conclusion\nBased on the analysis, the reported atomicity violation is valid because both ISRs can execute and modify shared variables without restrictions.\n\n### Final Report\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [15, 21, 15]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [15, 21, 15]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
